<title>USA: U.S. lead inventories down 26.9 pct in June - AMBS.</title>
<headline>U.S. lead inventories down 26.9 pct in June - AMBS.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lead stocks held by U.S. refiners fell to 12,184 short tons at the end of June, down 26.9 percent from May, and down 43.5 percent from June 1996, according to the American Bureau of Metal Statistics.</p>
<p>Production of lead totaled 31,618 tons, down 6.9 percent from May, but up 32.3 percent from June 1996.</p>
<p>Shipments from plants totaled 36,081 tons, down 7.8 percent from May, but up 35.2 percent from June 1996.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1646))</p>
